{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "planner_reply.v1",
  "title": "Planner reply",
  "$comment": "Draft v1 (MS-1, designed, not yet implemented). The planner reply for an edit with two or more source images; a request with one source image keeps planner_reply.v0. Same as planner_reply.v0 plus base_source_index (the image being edited; null only for subject_recompose, a rule code checks) and source_indexes on edit_targets, preserve, and on entities and attributes (null unless their source is source_image, which code checks). edit_kind is never null here: the task is edit. Source indexes are 1-based positions in the request order of the source images and exist only when the request holds two or more (decision 179). The schema checks what a schema can: integers of at least 1, a non-empty list, no repeats. Code, which knows n, checks each index is at most n and the list is ascending (MS-4). Code builds intent_ir.v1 and plan_result.v2 from it. Prompt: planner_v2 (draft). Design: tasks/active/MS-1-contracts-docs.md.",
